The '''Esports World Cup''' is a tournament series that was announced in late 2023, building off the previously established '''Gamers8''' series.

'''Free Fire''' was announced as part of the game titles line-up on February 22nd, 2024.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://twitter.com/ESWCgg/status/1760590256368206103|title=Takeoff authorized: Rio ➡️ Destination Riyadh 🛫|date=2024-02-22|author=Esports World Cup|language={{FlagNoLink|usuk}} ''English''}}</ref>
:''Click [https://liquipedia.net/esports/Esports_World_Cup/2024 here] to read more information about the Esports World Cup 2024 such as calendar, club standings and more.''

==About==
* July 14th - {{Team|LOUD}} and {{Team|Team Solid}} each received '''-5 points''' penalty points in the Grand Finals stage due to attempt of teaming.<ref name="loud & solid penalty">{{Cite web|url=https://x.com/EWC_EN/status/1812481913220644950 |title=Competitive ruling: Team Solid and LOUD.|publisher='''Esports World Cup'''|date=2024-07-14}}</ref>

